{
  "schema": "research-public-artifact/v1",
  "concept": "Salesforce Pub/Sub OAuth permissions entitlements and allocations",
  "slug": "salesforce-pub-sub-oauth-permissions-entitlements-and-allocations",
  "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1330214025185617832abec1f5667e19a87a0692dce1f2e69b858e7291b55287",
  "canonical_artifact_sha256": "ed79511c96821b05db1ccf575f33cdb9e5f436d3d6a13b2cbb28cf8869a2eba7",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:016b20c959b0fc9a1ca916ee73debe5798851c800ddc7feea817bf051c7a10b0",
      "text": "The integration user needs API Enabled; Axual specifically requires this permission on the Run As User for its client credentials flow. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-rest/guide/intro-rest-compatible-editions.html",
      "also": [
        "https://docs.axual.io/axual/2026.3/components/run-time/kafka-connect/connect-plugins-catalog/plugins-made-by-axual/salesforce-pubsub-source/index.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:35a3e68dd7ef6c49cb8d353e5d1206d9cd03a572c850b4eaeb73b47c55304330",
        "ev:da9bf7b3679c0b96f0f556d2c5256d8fe6470df439ae79c0eeea91a3fac50f7d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:cc1a178b404253aefaa0a3b952099fb276959a308010347f3bebb22a7bc07300",
      "text": "For a specific standard or custom object that supports View All Records, CDC requires that permission for the object. Standard objects without it, such as Task and Event, require View All Data. The table lists View All Data for all entities on a channel, plus View All Users when User is included. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/change-data-capture/guide/cdc-security-perms.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:b07ac949148f5abbe0309d4e9f28c4d7fbb0d924912ba462a114715eca88b9ca"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:6b8731b0f160a357e57e693fada2ab5e846a7e17583d241708abd7517f96353a",
      "text": "For single-entity standard CDC channels, Salesforce checks the object permission when subscribing and denies insufficient access. For the standard /data/ChangeEvents channel and custom channels, Salesforce enforces permissions on event delivery and enforces permission changes within 10 minutes for Pub/Sub API subscribers. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/change-data-capture/guide/cdc-security-perms.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:e0d87c79c025ce271378af21457d8eaf153ccb37c04f14632ceb4d147dc87ad1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:1cf0e71c5283e5a0933f6b48ccaabdffdfd3b03e80595a7f8c2e51d9d2ab69ff",
      "text": "Axual documents client credentials and JWT bearer as its two machine-to-machine Pub/Sub authentication flows; client credentials uses a Run As User and JWT requires the integration user to be pre-authorized. This describes that connector, not an exhaustive Salesforce flow list. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-03)",
      "source_url": "https://docs.axual.io/axual/2026.3/components/run-time/kafka-connect/connect-plugins-catalog/plugins-made-by-axual/salesforce-pubsub-source/index.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:adea39d07eaf224dbdfbe2da114e134e3fd9f2c17981ff4cb7d16f486b0be347"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:8391fcdbb241dcaa56a683636d1649e70eaf54949335d8a42a1f89da2b51a4a6",
      "text": "The OAuth client credentials flow does not issue a refresh token or support UI sessions; Salesforce filters out `full`, `web`, and `refresh_token, offline_access` scopes for this flow. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=xcloud.remoteaccess_oauth_client_credentials_flow_ca.htm&language=en_US&type=5",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:14209a90d2e436093552b0eab0eaf8fd4773c39e9f0880da39bfdbaaaef4f631"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:a65f620dcf5f973b2ef9061cfeaf873c3c8e2ce601b4bd6a06a6c95651c1a5e8",
      "text": "Across outstanding FetchRequests or ManagedFetchRequests in one Subscribe or ManagedSubscribe call, the maximum requested-event count is 100; Salesforce treats larger requested counts as 100. This flow-control ceiling is separate from the org\u2019s event-delivery allocation. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/allocations.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:4a22feb30db7a5e650ff0f4302376947724f6a8979a17dcd0a3525ebdfb495d8",
        "ev:70892704202c6a6f69cebd3510a6462f9a040412989e36f6047fb10230e0aab4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:7ce76da06a78945dd9933ae57d15f45fb52981a4707f023a1b02f696d739c862",
      "text": "Exceeding the default delivery allocation disconnects the subscription. Pub/Sub API reports `sfdc.platform.eventbus.grpc.subscription.limit.exceeded` with `You have exceeded the event delivery limit for your org`. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/platform-events/guide/platform-events-limits-default.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:ad7beba56b1e9d2508dc24c0bb4a10c70bb5ca587d6194a2a649f9501106b9ae"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:24f19cd73e41902944055beaf51465d0b6b4464ab16353eae31bd654eb06ea5a",
      "text": "Salesforce documents a maximum of 100 outstanding requested events across FetchRequests in a Subscribe call, whereas Axual says Salesforce supports 10,000 events per request in its connector batch-size documentation. Treat these as conflicting source statements; size RPC demand using the primary Salesforce limit and distinguish connector poll batching from wire requests. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/allocations.html",
      "also": [
        "https://docs.axual.io/axual/2026.3/components/run-time/kafka-connect/connect-plugins-catalog/plugins-made-by-axual/salesforce-pubsub-source/index.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:70892704202c6a6f69cebd3510a6462f9a040412989e36f6047fb10230e0aab4",
        "ev:d7d160006b7097cba97e20e7be0f5454fd7836271bad42ff4b0c6a5d968238c0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:2eb1ed092f69639defbe9b98d989a10906abba17af69f2bf8dd691b508cf8659",
      "text": "Pub/Sub API accepts an OAuth access token or Salesforce session ID; each RPC supplies authentication metadata named `accesstoken`, `instanceurl`, and `tenantid`. WSO2\u2019s connector independently documents supplying the access token, instance URL, and organization ID. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/supported-auth.html",
      "also": [
        "https://mi.docs.wso2.com/en/4.5.0/reference/connectors/sf-pubsub-inbound/sf-pubsub-inbound-endpoint-example/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:c0fd8a1667492d5bc4b175ac31fd93a2551f269d078a845e8498bf0a253f69cd",
        "ev:ee0a8619d00d4fd14df95a88b592bba2d9a0c8e7075a2d3d327729e324bfe8e4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:1d4b30ad94d635872320152088010a61e66d3ca9b1b45c61382a6e5e61a5d85a",
      "text": "The current Pub/Sub guide lists Enterprise, Performance, Unlimited, and Developer Editions and excludes Government Cloud; validate Pub/Sub entitlement separately from successful OAuth authentication. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/intro.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:da1bfbeb934341cf68f643aad5472a34b9b62a8013f65033a0c5cbb17fe69bfd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:07daaaaa6fcede6a6fc84b8ef5e6e38001a97c143fa08e7133a3e50fd368edaa",
      "text": "Creating connected apps is restricted as of Spring \u201926. Existing connected apps remain usable, while Salesforce recommends external client apps for new integrations; creating further connected apps requires contacting Salesforce Support. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-rest/guide/intro-oauth-and-connected-apps.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:65cc2a00bf8d64eec67f0ca099b136cd18da61da43b996c61bf229c0d4f4591b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:6805d6e1fff782f67f76058a54577b523e6467ad208e8048faa39e2f5880dbb7",
      "text": "Event deliveries are counted per subscribed client and added across subscribers; a new subscriber consumes additional delivery allocation for the same event. The default pool is shared by high-volume platform events and CDC. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/platform-events/guide/platform-events-limits-default.html",
      "also": [
        "https://jamforce.nz/blog/platform-event-limit/",
        "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/allocations.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:22d47d16204891abe160d5ece4e1bc6153731f8c46daa70694e8ce02aa9f9907",
        "ev:30f7ec093508511d45ccf39710132fb7b010e63de77db93fefcb91130e044f66",
        "ev:5f3d89edb9eda095808eaf084794b6c73a0627f27a0b29b4d464aa70f19f0f90"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:c71390d8d78232b144c63719245bc2d85168c4c8b751a2c644c24251a6599b1a",
      "text": "For orgs without add-ons, documented default delivery allocations over the last 24 hours are 50,000 for Performance/Unlimited, 25,000 for Enterprise/Professional with API add-on, and 10,000 for Developer. Add-ons move delivery usage to a monthly entitlement model; confirm the actual org entitlement before sizing. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/platform-events/guide/platform-events-limits-default.html",
      "also": [
        "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/intro.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:7582aa44a72cd0f0648c79c2a851fff0673a0d6c3020f912c1f564afe4603cdf",
        "ev:7902c8a515cb798510c80595b37069807dbe6440425a7f916f6594500c3a3a93"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:1f39cc789b3e4bae8a5f19b2f98bd89afe56e76074d033c5907f5b63457042cc",
      "text": "The current Pub/Sub allocation page caps unique managed subscriptions at 200 per Salesforce org. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/allocations.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:b71900e79d9a4923a8cce068b891307d683f45afe7dedb1ce2344d68e3fb16c7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:ccd0c2ea0e712739b1ce1acbb2cb6a6e7268000145aaaaeed60d227c33977a93",
      "text": "James Winter reports an incident in which an overnight EmpApi browser subscription consumed the shared delivery allocation while Apex log processing continued. This is a first-person account about an API subscriber, not a measured Pub/Sub outage. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://jamforce.nz/blog/platform-event-limit/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:66a1bb445988f5f21ad2d22262db24c6214406a5010be83bd6e1296017488050",
        "ev:7b6182c30b062d974bd042aefb9aec48f2057918f2bec60bda70ee3076a913b2",
        "ev:bcd0e3fdb39dafca1780fe4df1c1e025b7e8c07243ed69cbb06156a750920749"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:c2c2ae6361469e0e67977aa38a553465ca2f8ec6db74217d8c383083098dde33",
      "text": "Salesforce API access requires API access enabled for both the org and user, including the user\u2019s API Enabled permission. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-rest/guide/intro-rest-compatible-editions.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:c5771f3870706fc9a1ef8cc5aaf673b109b4b74d71e2204d6d8c7084ca50813f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:e0a7a45761a151354fe72db5c05c1efdebf985de7d612ecc518d89293d4dcf40",
      "text": "A platform-event add-on moves event delivery to monthly usage-based entitlement and permits daily spikes through a grace allocation. Salesforce can adjust grace allocations; purchasing an add-on does not promise unlimited delivery. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/platform-events/guide/platform-events-limits-entitlement.html",
      "also": [
        "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/platform-events/guide/platform-events-limits-default.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:7582aa44a72cd0f0648c79c2a851fff0673a0d6c3020f912c1f564afe4603cdf",
        "ev:a3d5979f67d86f3e30627ff4d3c74678211539c6a5c240a5b148d3e4db66c4a4",
        "ev:c6f60ea7b0f39f9a50b5d6dee3a7ae6f2614a60ef522002031e7dd59f407dd96"
      ]
    }
  ],
